ivileges at certain amenities at the Kapalua Resort. Maui Land & Pineapple Company, Inc. was incorporated in 1909 and is based in Lahaina, Hawaii.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Race A. Randle | Chief Executive Officer | Age 43 | Compensation: $551,430 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 20 people. Revenue per employee of $973K ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers. Stock-based compensation of $216K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Maui Land & Pineapple Company,  is a micro-cap real estate business with a $275M market cap on $19M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and -2% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -12% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $484,000 of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 22% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 69% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Real Estate peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 